course: dictionary
lesson: 6968
title: The pancreas
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: An organ is a part of the body that does a special job. The pancreas is an organ in your belly, behind your stomach.
explain: The pancreas makes two important things. It makes digestive juices, which go into the small intestine to break down food. It also makes insulin, a hormone that controls how much sugar is in your blood.
explain: Context helps you here. «The pancreas makes insulin.» The sentence tells you that insulin is something the pancreas makes, so it is probably something important for the body.
explain: «In type 1 diabetes the immune system has destroyed the insulin-making cells of the pancreas, an organ behind the stomach.» The words after the comma explain the word pancreas: it is an organ behind the stomach.
fact: Pancreas is a noun. Its plural is pancreases.
fact: The pancreas is an organ in the belly, behind the stomach.
fact: The pancreas makes digestive juices and the hormone insulin.
fact: Insulin lets sugar from food into cells for energy.
fact: In type 1 diabetes, the pancreas does not make enough insulin, so people take insulin by injection or pump.
exercise: «The pancreas is an organ behind the stomach.» Where is the pancreas? | In the chest, next to the heart | In the head, behind the eyes | In the leg, near the knee | *In the belly, behind the stomach
exercise: «In type 1 diabetes the immune system has destroyed the insulin-making cells of the pancreas.» What does the pancreas make that controls sugar in the blood? | *Insulin | Blood | Stomach acid | Bone
exercise: «The pancreas sends juices into the small intestine to break down food.» What does the pancreas send into the small intestine? | *Digestive juices | Blood cells | Air | Water only
test: Which hormone, made by the pancreas, controls the amount of sugar in the blood? | Keratin | Haemoglobin | Adrenaline | *Insulin
test: If the pancreas does not make enough insulin, what condition might a person have? | Asthma | *Type 1 diabetes | A cold | Measles
exam: Where in the body is the pancreas, and what does it make? | In the lungs, and it makes air | Under the skin of the arm, and it makes sweat | In the brain, and it makes memories | *Behind the stomach, and it makes digestive juices and insulin
